Richard,

Right now, the only workaround would be to remove the `Repository: Bioconductor` field from the downloaded ComplexHeatmap package.

On Fri, Oct 23, 2015 at 10:57 AM, Kevin Ushey <ke...@rstudio.com> wrote:
> I just downloaded ComplexHeatmap from Bioconductor and it indeed sets both `Repository: Bioconductor` and `biocViews: ...` in its DESCRIPTION.
>
> However, I do not see `Repository: Bioconductor` set in other new BioC packages; so I think the right change here is to either check and allow for `Repository: Bioconductor`, or check `biocViews` before validating the Repository field.
>
> We might also want to follow up with the BioC guys to see what they think.
>
> On Fri, Oct 23, 2015 at 10:49 AM, Tareef Kawaf <tar...@rstudio.com> wrote:
> > If this is a new standard, it will definitely be easier.  I know we have some work in flight that will make it much easier to support custom repositories so we can expand the footprint from the current CRAN, BioC, Github triumverate.
> >
> > On Fri, Oct 23, 2015 at 1:47 PM, Joe Cheng <j...@rstudio.com> wrote:
> > > I'm guessing Bioconductor recently changed their build process to tag their DESCRIPTION files like this? If so it's actually slightly nicer for us in the long run, isn't it? (i.e. we can eventually trust Repository: Bioconductor instead of relying on the biocViews field)
> > >
> > > On Fri, Oct 23, 2015 at 10:43 AM Tareef Kawaf <tar...@rstudio.com> wrote:
> > > > Richard,
> > > > Is there any chance you installed this package from a source other than BioConductor?  Would it be too much trouble to try installing it from BioConductor again to see if that resolves the issue?
